diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive end-to-end testing no network fault was found. The wireless gateway (HSRP-equivalent VIP 10.6.0.1 on dswa2.br0.40, VLAN 40) is fully operational. laptop1 holds the correct IP address (10.6.0.100/24) and default route, and can reach every host and subnet in the topology: the local gateway, all office VLANs (10.1–10.6.x), the DNS server at 10.5.0.4, and the ISP-side interface at 203.0.113.1 — all with zero packet loss. OSPF is fully converged on all devices (r1, csw1/2, dswa1/2, dswb1/2), routing tables are correct, and r1's MASQUERADE NAT rules cover 10.6.0.0/24. The STP-blocked uplink on aswa1.eth3 is expected behavior in a dual-uplink topology without LAG; traffic flows normally via aswa1.eth2→dswa1→peer-bond→dswa2. The DNS server on srv1 deliberately operates with recursion disabled (the named.conf comment states "Offline lab: no upstream, so recursion is off"), so queries for public names such as google.com are refused by design. Internal zone lookups (*.jeremysitlab.com) do resolve correctly. There is no web server deployed anywhere in the topology. The user's symptom — "nothing loads" — arises entirely from this being an offline lab with no actual internet connectivity and no application-layer web service, not from any fault in the network infrastructure. The IT technician's suspicion that "the wireless gateway might have gone" is incorrect; the gateway is fully healthy. No corrective action is required on the network.
=== END ===